Z||000000||varnster||02-13-2001||08:57 PM||||now that mr mike no longer sells the carpet kits how do I remove and recarpet my doors,<BR>allso I tore a clip right out of the press board when I took the panel off, any repair<BR>advise. thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||02-13-2001||09:18 PM||||Take the door panel off , Get glovev (nice heavy ones) soak the carpet in WD-40 , it pulls off a lot easier...<P>Where you go from their is up to you.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan M McCreery<BR>86 GT<BR>New Custom White face gauges 17" Tr motorsports Typhoons Ground Control coil overs , Big bars front and rear , Mustang scoop , accel coil , no cat , 4spd , short shift , poly dog bone and bushings momo pedals and shift knob , round headlight conversion , Geni stainless steel oval exhaust tips. Pioneer 6000 CD player , Sony Mobile Amp. Currently doing big brake conversion...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/jssig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||02-13-2001||09:18 PM||||well, sitting here looking at one of my spare panels, it looks to me that the carpet is only glued on.  I can't find any sort of fasteners.  But then again, they might be hidden in the carpet itself.  It looks as if it would be easy to remove the carpet from the front, but it seems to me that the backside of the carpet is glued on a little better.  I guess, try very carefully, to use a utility knife to work the carpet loose from the cardboard backing.<BR>As for the retainer holder, I would just epoxy in a new one in the same spot.  It doesnt matter whether they stay in there or not when you take off the door panel in the first place.<P>Hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tom88gt||02-13-2001||10:47 PM||||Use epoxy to repair the door clips.  Use the 5 minute stuff.  Mix a little.  Spread it on the door panel where the clip tore out.  Press the clip back in place.  Let it dry.  Reinstall door panel.  If you remove the panel again it will tear again because the clip holds too well.  So you have to reglue it everytime you remove the door panel.  But the repair holds very well.  ||||reg||4
Z||000004||gabriel||02-14-2001||05:26 AM||||I think that the whole setup with the christmas tress (interior trim clips) w/ cardboard panels is freaking annoying, but all manufacturers use them, I believe.<P>  I wouldn't do that epoxy thing myself, but I have had good results using fiberglasss resin on the panels to stiffen them.  Don't do this with the clips in.  After it has hardened, then put them in & re - install normally.  You will be able to reuse the panels & you can get new trees at any auto store.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||02-14-2001||07:29 AM||||If you use the panel removal tool you are less likely to rip the Christmas Tree clips off.  I got one from WalMart for about $5.<BR>However, the tool does not work well for the clip in the middle of the door panel. <P>I use Hot Glue to replace the clips.  It sets almost immediately and you can goop it up to whaever thickness you need.  So far so good. <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000006||William||02-14-2001||04:32 PM||||Speaking of door panels, Have any of you guys noticed that your door panels have become slightly wavy on the bottom edge? Both mine are that way and so are the ones in the junk yards, (they are not perfectly flat in the carpeted area). I'm gonna be installing new carpet and leather uppers this weekend. Is it possible to find better panels before I restore mine or have ALL of them become kinda wavy over the years?||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-15-2001||07:53 PM||||If the carpet is just dirty and not actually damaged badly then try cleaning it with spray foam carpet cleaner and work it with a brush. If it's oil/grease try some 409 or basin,tub,and tile cleaner.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tom88gt||02-16-2001||10:21 PM||||I'm guessing that the torn clip is the metal one at the top and not the plastic type.  So gluing is the only fix I know of.||||reg||1
